3. Meta Model API outputs (SAM 3.1, Muse Spark 1.3)
   Boxes, tracks and replies were produced through the Meta Model API by CairoFlow's requests;
   under the Model API Terms of Service (section 4.1) the requester owns inputs and outputs.
   SAM output is acknowledged as SAM 3.1 output wherever it is published (the SAM licence asks
   for acknowledgement). Model output is labelled model-generated and is never used as a
   measured result. cache/muse/NOTICE.md points at a compliance note that is not here; the term
   it relies on is the one named in this section.
   cache/muse/ holds four replies to one request. The first has its x-ratelimit-* header values
   removed. The three repeats (.r2 to .r4) keep them as received, because records pin those
   files; they are request and token quota figures, not credentials.

4. Software used, not redistributed
   Eclipse SUMO (EPL-2.0) and the Python packages pinned in uv.lock (each under its own licence)
   are installed from PyPI by the user; the npm packages pinned in apps/web/package-lock.json
   likewise. No third-party code is vendored in this repository.
   A built apps/web/dist bundles the fonts Barlow, Barlow Semi Condensed and IBM Plex Mono (SIL
   Open Font License 1.1), which come from the @fontsource npm packages.

5. Neural vehicle detectors (optional, not distributed here)
   No detector code or weights are in this repository. Each option below is installed by the
   person running it, through its extra, and its weights are downloaded at run time and checked
   against a SHA-256 pinned in the source.

   Default: D-FINE Large (Apache-2.0), the `vision` extra.
   Weights: ustc-community/dfine-large-obj2coco-e25 on Hugging Face, run through the transformers
   library (Apache-2.0). PyTorch and torchvision (BSD-style licences) come from
   download.pytorch.org.

   Opt-in: ultralytics and the VisDrone YOLO26s weights (AGPL-3.0), the `vision-agpl` extra.
   Weights: dronefreak/visdrone-yolo26s on Hugging Face. Neither is imported or loaded unless
   chosen, with CAIROFLOW_DETECTOR=visdrone-yolo26s. Running with this option makes that combined
   runtime subject to AGPL-3.0, including section 13's duty to offer source to users who interact
   with it over a network. CairoFlow's own source stays under the MIT licence in LICENSE, but a
   deployment that uses this option must meet AGPL-3.0 as a whole. Anyone who cannot should use
   the default. The sample analyses data/sample/analyses/cv-ngsim-int2-15min-study/ and
   data/sample/analyses/cv-hero-sam/ were produced with this option, and their records say so.

   Evaluated only: the bake-off also scored rfdetr-m and rtdetrv2-r50, and its record says how
   they did. Neither is distributed here or used by CairoFlow.
